INT. ROOFTOP GREENHOUSE, GRAND HOTEL - NIGHT

Glass walls. Orchids in hanging baskets. Rain tapping overhead. A city smeared into color below.

DET. SOLANO, 40s, trench coat, sits on a wrought-iron bench, hands in his pockets. HESTER VANCE, 50s, the hotel manager, waters ferns with a copper can. KIERAN, 20s, the night porter, hovers near the door. MR. BAPTISTE, 60s, an elderly guest in a silk robe, studies an orchid.

A STRANGER, 30s, wet hair, black jacket, steps in. Nods to no one. Stands apart.

SOLANO
Evening.

STRANGER
Evening.

SOLANO
You're not a guest.

STRANGER
I'm waiting for someone.

SOLANO
Who?

STRANGER
A friend.

HESTER
(not looking up)
The greenhouse closes at eleven.

STRANGER
It's ten-forty.

HESTER
Then you have twenty minutes.

KIERAN
Sir, can I take your coat?

STRANGER
No.

SOLANO
What's your friend's name?

STRANGER
You wouldn't know him.

SOLANO
Try me.

STRANGER
Calder.

BAPTISTE
(without turning)
Calder is dead.

STRANGER
Is he?

BAPTISTE
I buried him in March.

STRANGER
Then who's standing here?

Silence. The rain. A drop falls from a leaf onto the tile.

CALDER
(the Stranger, now)
Mr. Baptiste. It's been a long time.

BAPTISTE
Not long enough.

CALDER
I came to return something.

SOLANO
(low)
Hester. Clear the room.

HESTER
Detective?

SOLANO
Now.

KIERAN
Sir, I --

SOLANO
Out, son.

Kieran backs out of the greenhouse. Hester sets the can down, walks to the door. Locks it from the outside.

CALDER
Don't be dramatic.

SOLANO
You're supposed to be in a box.

CALDER
So is he.

BAPTISTE
(turning at last)
What did you bring me?

CALDER
Your watch.

He pulls it from his jacket. Gold. Heavy. Holds it up by the chain.

CALDER (CONT'D)
You gave it to me the night you shot me.

BAPTISTE
I gave it to you as a kindness.

CALDER
It stopped at eleven.

BAPTISTE
It always did.

Solano rises. His hand is out of his pocket now.

SOLANO
Mr. Calder, put the watch on the bench.

CALDER
It's not for the bench.

SOLANO
Put it down.

CALDER
Detective, I've waited eight months. I can wait one more minute.

The watch swings. Tick. Tick. Tick.

It stops.

CALDER (CONT'D)
Eleven.
